          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em BGG resolution
            is a certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+resolution"} projective resolution
            of certain
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
          %p
            More in detail, give a finite dimensional semisimple complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+subalgebra"} Cartan subalgebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔥
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{h}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/root+system"} root system
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo +
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔥
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^+\subset \mathfrak{h}^*
            be the set of dominant integral
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weights"} weights
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda\in P^+
            consider the corresponding finite dimensional left
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\mathfrak{g})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(\lambda)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolutions"} resolutions
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(\lambda)
            are defined in a series of papers of Bernstein, Gel’fand and Gel’fand (
            %a{:href => "#BBG7x"}> BBG 7x
            ) and are now called
            = succeed "." do
              %em BGG resolutions
          %p
            These resolutions have a natural incarnation in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complexes"} complexes
            of sections of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tractor+bundles"} tractor bundles
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag+varieties"} flag varieties
            or more generally over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homogeneous+space"} homogeneous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parabolic+geometry"} parabolic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein+geometries"} Klein geometries
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parabolic+geometry"} parabolic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometries"} Cartan geometries
            = succeed "." do
              %em curved BGG sequences
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#CalderbankDiemer00"} Calderbank-Diemer 00, theorem 3.6
          %p
            BGG resolutions may be used to construct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolutions"} resolutions
            of sheaves of constant functions on
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein+geometries"} Klein geometries
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            that are more efficient (smaller) that the general resolution given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            (the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincare+lemma"} Poincare lemma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leray+spectral+sequences"} Leray spectral sequences
            as they appear in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Penrose+transforms"} Penrose transforms
            (
            %a{:href => "#BastonEastwood89"}> Baston-Eastwood 89, chapter 8
            ).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#curved_structure
            Curved
            = succeed "-Structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
          %p
            Under a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product"} cup product
            the BGG sequence becomes a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curved+A-infinity+algebra"} curved A-infinity algebra
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#CalderbankDiemer00"} Calderbank-Diemer 00, section 6
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verma+module"} Verma module
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parabolic+geometry"} parabolic geometry
          %h2#references References
          %h3#original_case_over_flag_variety Original case over flag variety
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eom"}> eom
                \: Alvany Rocha,
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.encyclopediaofmath.org/index.php?title=BGG_resolution&oldid=14028"} BGG resolution
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category_O"} category O
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+N.+Bernstein"}> Joseph N. Bernstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Israel+M.+Gelfand"} Israel M. Gelfand
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+I.+Gelfand"} Sergei I. Gelfand
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Differential operators on the base affine space and a study of
                    = succeed "-modules" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝔤
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lie groups and their representations
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.tau.ac.il/~bernstei/Publication_list/publication_texts/BGG-differ-operators.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BGG.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#BBG7x
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+N.+Bernstein"}> Joseph N. Bernstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Israel+M.+Gelfand"} Israel M. Gelfand
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+I.+Gelfand"} Sergei I. Gelfand
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Structure of representations generated by vectors of highest weight
                = succeed ":" do
                  %strong 5
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A certain category of -modules
                = succeed ":" do
                  %strong 10
            %li
              %p
                James E. Humphreys,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Representations of semisimple Lie algebras in the BGG category
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒪
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.umass.edu/~jeh/bgg/main.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
          %ul
            %li
              M. Falk,
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Vladimir Schechtman
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Vladimir+Schechtman"} ?
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Varchenko"} Alexander Varchenko
              %em BGG resolutions via configuration spaces
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1309.7811"}> arxiv/1309.7811
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %blockquote
            %p
              We study the blow-ups of configuration spaces. These spaces have a structure of what we call an Orlik-Solomon manifold; it allows us to compute the intersection cohomology of certain flat connections with logarithmic singularities using some Aomoto type complexes of logarithmic forms. Using this construction we realize geometrically the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sl
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sl_2
              Bernstein - Gelfand - Gelfand resolution as an Aomoto complex.
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Sergey Arkhipov,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A new construction of the semi-infinite BGG resolution
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9605043"} q-alg/9605043
          %p
            Discussion in the context of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Penrose+transform"} Penrose transform
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Michael Eastwood,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Variations on the de Rham complex
                %strong 46
                (1999), no. 11, 1368–1376
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/notices/199911/fea-eastwood.pdf"} pdf
            %li#BastonEastwood89
              %p
                R. J. Baston, M. G. Eastwood,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Penrose transform
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet/search/publdoc.html?r=1&pg1=CNO&s1=1038279"} MR92j:32112
          %h3#ReferencesCurved Curved generalization to parabolic Cartan geometries
          %p
            The generalization from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+spaces"} coset spaces
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parabolic+geometry"} parabolic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometries"} Cartan geometries
            (curved BGG sequences) is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Baston90
              %p
                R. J. Baston,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Verma modules and differential conformal invariants
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+%C4%8Cap"}> Andreas Čap
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Slov%C3%A1k"} Jan Slovák
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladim%C3%ADr+Sou%C4%8Dek"} Vladimír Souček
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Bernstein-Gelfand-Gelfand sequences
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+%C4%8Cap"}> Andreas Čap
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Slov%C3%A1k"} Jan Slovák
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladim%C3%ADr+Sou%C4%8Dek"} Vladimír Souček
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Bernstein-Gelfand-Gelfand sequences
                = succeed ":1" do
                  %strong 154
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/3062111"} jstor
            %li#CalderbankDiemer00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Calderbank"}> David Calderbank
                , Tammo Diemer,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential invariants and curved Bernstein-Gelfand-Gelfand sequences
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0001158"} arXiv:math/0001158
            %li#CapSoucek07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+%C4%8Cap"}> Andreas Čap
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladim%C3%ADr+Sou%C4%8Dek"} Vladimír Souček
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Curved Casimir operators and the BGG machinery
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 3
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0708.3180"} arxiv:0708.3180
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.3842/SIGMA.2007.111"} doi
          .property
            category:
            %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/representation+theory"} representation theory
